WHY["Decode pods are the final response point for user traffic.\nThe routing sidecar receives the EPP decision, coordinates prefill, waits for KV handoff, then forwards to local vLLM.\nThat keeps the external routing contract stable while hiding the internal P/D choreography behind one decode endpoint."]:::note
POD["Decode Pod"]:::tag
EPP["EPP decision"]:::orange2
KV["KV handoff"]:::prefill
SIDECAR["Routing sidecar\nport 5000"]:::decode
PROXY["proxy to local"]:::plain
VLLM["Local decode vLLM\nport 5001"]:::teal
NOTE["decode pod = coordination point + final response point"]:::note2

EPP --> SIDECAR
KV -.-> SIDECAR
SIDECAR --> PROXY
PROXY --> VLLM
POD -.-> SIDECAR
POD -.-> VLLM
VLLM -.-> NOTE

